WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:02.440
It's not easy being a superhero.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.350
If we mess up, it might ruin our day.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.850
If Wonder Woman does, then it's a complete
and utter disaster.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.510
Here are the worst things Wonder Woman has
ever done.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.699
Way back in Wonder Woman #1, written and drawn
by her creators William Moulton Marston and

00:00:14.699 --> 00:00:19.030
Harry Peter, Diana makes her humble debut
by briefly joining the circus.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.470
It's an opportunity for her to show off what
she can do to a world that's still getting

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.470
to know her.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:26.640
Of course this was in the old days, before
most people realized what a bad place the

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.470
circus is for animals.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:32.320
In the 21st century, there have been public
discussions about how horses, lions, and elephants

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.980
are mistreated by circuses, as they're made
to do things they were never meant to do,

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.660
like jump through rings of fire.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.600
This has led to many circuses either swearing
off the use of animals or going out of business

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.600
entirely.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.460
But in the 1940s, nobody cared.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.489
So there's Wonder Woman, picking up a horse
by its legs.

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:51.510
Then she literally wrestles a lion, tossing
him several feet onto his back in his cage,

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.960
while saying "I don't want to hurt him."

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.970
Yes, perhaps it's unfair to judge Wonder Woman
for behavior that was considered acceptable

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:57.970
at the time.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:01.450
On the other hand, this is Wonder Woman, who
journeyed from Paradise Island to Man's World

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.750
to spread peace and teach a better way to
live.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.049
Maybe if that's your goal, don't spend your
first chance to make an impression on people

00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:08.200
throwing lions around.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.899
A number of stories have teased a relationship
between Batman and Wonder Woman, but the idea

00:01:12.899 --> 00:01:15.970
was first raised in 1968's The Brave and the
Bold #78.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:20.979
In a story by Bob Haney and Bob Brown, Diana
and Batgirl duke it out in the Gotham City

00:01:20.979 --> 00:01:24.380
skies after professing their love for Batman
via skywriting.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:26.319
And it only gets weirder from there.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:29.389
The two heroines have a contest to win Batman's
heart.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:33.369
Wonder Woman showers Batman with gifts from
Paradise Island, while Batgirl gets him a

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:35.829
"groovy" new cape to cover his "brawny shoulders."

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:39.060
Wonder Woman responds by carving a Batman
statue out of gold.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.459
Both women get him a diamond-studded utility
belt.

00:01:41.459 --> 00:01:45.579
Then, the supervillain Copperhead attacks
and Batman springs into action, revealing

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:49.990
that the feud between his two allies was just
a ruse to make Copperhead think he was distracted.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:51.840
But the issue is only half over.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.170
Both women realize they've fallen in love
with Batman for real, and the battle continues.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:00.109
Both women give Batman clues to their secret
identities and then they drop all pretense

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:01.689
and just start punching each other.

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:05.599
Wonder Woman has Batgirl on the ropes when
everyone remembers Copperhead is still loose,

00:02:05.599 --> 00:02:07.520
and Wonder Woman takes off to stop him.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:11.700
The heroes bring Copperhead down together,
which somehow cures Wonder Woman and Batgirl

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.360
of their romantic rivalry.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.670
To quote another DC superhero:

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:16.670
"Hah!

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:19.910
Well, that was, haha, outrageous."

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.700
Wonder Woman and Superman is also a popular
pairing.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.240
However, the difference is that while Batman
may have a number of women who are interested

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:31.190
in him, Superman is known for having one true
love: Lois Lane.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:35.170
Depending on the continuity of the moment,
she might be his girlfriend or his wife.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.500
Unfortunately, that's never stopped Wonder
Woman from longing to be with him.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:43.320
This was especially true in George Pérez's
Wonder Woman Vol. 2 run in the late 1980s,

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:47.180
which happened to correspond to a time when
Clark's relationship with Lois was particularly

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.180
strong.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:52.300
Nonetheless, Diana had recurring dreams about
liaisons with the Man of Steel, culminating

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.271
in an actual date between the two.

00:02:54.271 --> 00:02:57.880
They never went farther than a passionate
kiss, but it was a kiss neither ever forgot.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:03.170
Unlike Batman or Superman, Wonder Woman has
never really had a strict no-killing policy.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:06.640
She's an Amazon warrior, and she'll kill if
she feels like it's necessary.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.980
For example, when the villainous Maxwell Lord
uses his mind-control abilities to turn Superman

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.780
into a weapon of mass destruction, Diana is
left with no option but to snap Lord's neck,

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:16.780
killing him instantly.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:22.310
In Wonder Woman #219's aftermath, the execution
is broadcast all over the world via Batman's

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:25.340
Brother Eye satellite, which Lord has commandeered.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.020
After witnessing the disturbing footage, the
public loses its faith in Wonder Woman — as

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.730
do Batman and Superman.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:34.930
Brother Eye rallies its bionic soldiers, the
OMACs, to extract revenge on Diana and the

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:35.980
other Amazons.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.821
A group of superheroes trapped in a pocket
dimension, who see the killing unfold, are

00:03:39.821 --> 00:03:44.330
so disgusted by the state of the world's heroes
that they try to rewrite reality itself, sparking

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:48.730
the Infinite Crisis crossover event and causing
upheaval in DC's entire continuity.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:53.569
In ancient Greece, hiketeia was a ritual in
which a person in trouble could seek asylum

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:56.200
by supplicating themselves to a potential
protector.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:00.440
In DC Comics, it's the title of a critically
acclaimed Wonder Woman graphic novel.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:05.440
Written by Greg Rucka with art by J.G. Jones,
Wonder Woman: The Hiketeia finds Diana granting

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:09.760
a young woman named Danielle Wellys asylum
after the girl performs the ritual, but there's

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:14.750
a problem: Danielle is wanted for killing
several men, and Batman is hot on her tail.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:18.209
By the time Diana learns what Danielle has
done, she's already accepted the girl's plea

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:21.430
for help, which puts her in a precarious situation.

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:24.620
Danielle's motivation for the killings is
sympathetic, but Wonder Woman couldn't break

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.620
the promise of the hiketeia regardless, because
that would both tarnish her honor and invoke

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.669
the wrath of the Furies, powerful entities
who enforce such agreements.

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:35.400
Unsurprisingly, Batman doesn't care about
any of that.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.650
He's just trying to bring a killer to justice.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:41.620
That leads to one of the most famous hero
vs. hero fights in DC Comics history, in which

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.150
Wonder Woman absolutely wrecks Batman.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:47.719
Wonder Woman is ready to keep fighting to
protect Danielle, but the girl takes her own

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:50.590
life and releases Diana from the hiketeia
with her dying breath.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.990
In George Perez's 1987 reboot of Wonder Woman,
Diana has a mentor named Julia Kapatelis , a

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:59.850
Harvard professor and expert in Ancient Greece.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:04.040
Needing somewhere to stay after leaving Themyscira,
Wonder Woman moves in with Julia and her teenage

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.040
daughter Vanessa.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.870
Over the next several years, Julia becomes
like a second mother to Diana, and Vanessa

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.039
becomes very much like a little sister.

00:05:11.039 --> 00:05:15.419
However, the life of a superhero is fast-paced,
and Wonder Woman eventually has to leave Boston

00:05:15.419 --> 00:05:17.289
and have other adventures elsewhere.

00:05:17.289 --> 00:05:21.289
Vanessa Kapatelis feels abandoned by the big
sister she thought would be by her side for

00:05:21.289 --> 00:05:22.289
life.

00:05:22.289 --> 00:05:25.970
This leaves Vanessa open to be manipulated
by some of Wonder Woman's enemies.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:30.610
Building on her growing resentment of Diana,
they turn Vanessa into the cyborg Silver Swan,

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:32.719
and send her on a path of destruction.

00:05:32.719 --> 00:05:37.039
Using her new superpowers, Vanessa violently
vents her anger at Wonder Woman, and her jealousy

00:05:37.039 --> 00:05:41.360
of Cassie Sandsmark, another young ally of
Diana's who recently became Wonder Girl.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.189
Diana vows to save Vanessa, and eventually
does, but she has to concede that Vanessa

00:05:45.189 --> 00:05:49.020
has a point — she may have loved the girl
like a sister, but she wasn't there when Vanessa

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:51.009
needed her, and that had dire consequences.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:57.089
As part of the "DC Rebirth" event in 2016,
Greg Rucka retold Wonder Woman's origin.

00:05:57.089 --> 00:06:01.470
In this version, her first mentor and friend
in the United States was not Julia Kapatelis,

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:02.699
but Barbara Ann Minerva.

00:06:02.699 --> 00:06:07.180
Barbara Ann teaches Diana English and helps
her adapt to the world outside Themyscira.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:11.710
When Dr. Minerva leaves on an expedition to
learn the secrets of the god Urzkartaga, Diana

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:15.539
promises to come if her friend needs help,
reassuring Barbara Ann that she's only a cell

00:06:15.539 --> 00:06:16.620
phone message away.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:20.900
Barbara Ann does run into trouble, and does
need Wonder Woman's help, but when she calls,

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:22.220
Diana doesn't come.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:25.650
By the time Wonder Woman eventually finds
her in the jungle, Barbara Ann Minerva has

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:28.809
already been transformed into the feral, bloodthirsty
Cheetah.

00:06:28.809 --> 00:06:32.340
Diana tries to explain that she never got
the message, but it's too late.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:36.270
Diana wasn't there when her friend needed
her, and now her friend has become a monster.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.820
Needless to say, their friendship never really
recovers.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:43.180
Both Wonder Woman and Cheetah eventually realize
the missed call was a villain's fault, but

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:44.419
it doesn't solve the problem.

00:06:44.419 --> 00:06:48.469
If a superhero can't protect their loved ones,
then what's the point of being a superhero?

00:06:49.469 --> 00:06:52.099
In DC Comics, there's no greater villain than
Darkseid.

00:06:52.099 --> 00:06:56.469
The tyrant of Apokolips isn't just another
alien overlord; he's the very embodiment of

00:06:56.469 --> 00:06:57.469
evil.

00:06:57.469 --> 00:07:00.199
There's no doubt that Earth and the rest of
the galaxy would be better off without his

00:07:00.199 --> 00:07:01.199
influence.

00:07:01.199 --> 00:07:06.119
Nevertheless, in Wonder Woman Vol. 2 #173,
Diana gives up a part of her soul in order

00:07:06.119 --> 00:07:10.759
to restore Darkseid's power, giving him exactly
what he needs to continue his reign of terror.

00:07:10.759 --> 00:07:14.680
It happens as part of the "Our Worlds at War"
crossover, in which a team of superheroes

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:18.569
work together with President Lex Luthor and
his secret ally, Darkseid, to fend off an

00:07:18.569 --> 00:07:20.849
alien menace called Imperiex.

00:07:20.849 --> 00:07:24.990
After the battle, which leaves Diana's mother
Hippolyta and millions of others dead, Brainiac

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:29.960
13 launches an attack of its own, using the
planet-sized battle station Warworld to decimate

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.870
Apokolips and destroy Earth.

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:35.710
In order to save humanity, Wonder Woman needs
Darkseid's help — and the only way to get

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:37.650
it is to restore his missing powers.

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:41.800
The Amazons pray, while Raven of the Teen
Titans helps channel the Amazon's prayers

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.999
through Wonder Woman and into Darkseid.

00:07:43.999 --> 00:07:46.930
Before long, the god of evil's strength is
restored.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:51.440
That's enough to stop Brainiac 13 and Imperiex,
and to make sure that Darkseid remains a thorn

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:54.090
in the Justice League's side for years to
come.

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:55.379
It isn't all bad news, however.

00:07:55.379 --> 00:07:59.740
During the transfer, a small piece of Wonder
Woman's soul worms its way into Darkseid,

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.710
infecting him with one of Diana's most important
powers: compassion.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:08.350
The Injustice: Gods Among Us comic, like the
video game it's based on, is set in an alternate

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:12.089
reality, but it's one that's very close to
the main DC Universe.

00:08:12.089 --> 00:08:16.270
In Injustice, DC's characters have the same
origin stories as their mainstream versions.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:18.080
It's just a world where everything has gone
wrong.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:22.409
While Wonder Woman spends the bulk of the
series as Superman's ally — even as he slowly

00:08:22.409 --> 00:08:25.800
transforms into a despot— she seems to be
helping out for the right reasons.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:30.080
She regards Superman's use of force as a necessary
tool in the battle against evil.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:34.450
She helps track down Mirror Master, who kidnapped
Superman's adopted parents, but she doesn't

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:35.450
kill him.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:38.470
She relies on diplomacy to talk Aquaman out
of attacking the surface world.

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:42.740
However, when a superhero named Galaxor stands
up to Superman's regime, the Man of Steel

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:45.500
and Wonder Woman break his spine, crippling
him.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:49.940
In order to help a band of refugees, she crushes
a warlord's skull, then rounds up his armies

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:52.920
and lets the general's victims kill the oppressive
soldiers.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:57.530
Finally, when a group of rebel heroes team
up to defeat Superman once and for all, Wonder

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:01.650
Woman leaps into action, lashing out with
her lasso and snapping Huntress' neck.

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:02.980
After that, she's never the same.

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:07.680
In the reality of Injustice, Wonder Woman
may be a hero gone very wrong, but in the

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.840
timeline of Flashpoint, she's a straight-up
supervillain.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:14.320
Flashpoint starts with the Flash going back
in time to save his mother's life, but he

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.340
ends up wrecking the entire timeline, creating
a violent world with no Justice League, no

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:20.250
Bruce Wayne, and no hope.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:24.270
As a young princess on Themyscira, Diana gives
in to her urge for adventure and takes to

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:25.390
sea on a boat.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:28.350
She's attacked by a sea monster, but Aquaman
rescues her.

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:32.900
This leads to an alliance between Themyscira
and Atlantis, which is to be cemented by Diana

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.390
and Aquaman's wedding.

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:36.180
During the ceremony, Queen Hippolyta is murdered,
and the Atlanteans take the blame, leading

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.180
to all-out war.

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:41.150
In a last-ditch effort to decimate the Atlantean
forces, Wonder Woman and the Amazons destroy

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:44.380
Themyscira, killing thousands of soldiers,
and flee to Britain.

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:47.470
When they're denied asylum, they conquer instead,
renaming the U.K.

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:48.750
New Themyscira.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:53.450
Wonder Woman, now the queen, kills Aquaman's
lover Mera, and in response Atlantis floods

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.970
Europe, resulting in the death of millions.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:10:00.240
Before long, the rest of the world is consumed
by the Atlantean-Amazon conflict and the Flash

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:03.850
is forced to go back in time and let his mother
die in order to put everything back together.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:09.010
In the animated adaptation of Flashpoint,
Wonder Woman's behavior is even worse.

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:13.000
Much of the violence committed by the Amazon
army in the comics is done by Diana herself

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.000
in the movie.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.000
In short?

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.930
Whatever reality you're in, do not mess with
Wonder Woman.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:20.440
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:24.600
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
comic book histories are coming soon.

